<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">11082026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Tomorrow the moon's shadow crosses Iceland, northern Spain and the Mediterranean — mainland Europe's first total solar eclipse in nearly thirty years, with a deep partial phase over north Africa and the Middle East.</s> <s>Totality happens at all only because the sun is about four hundred times wider than the moon and about four hundred times further away, a coincidence with no physical cause and an expiry date, since the moon drifts away from us by roughly four centimetres a year.</s> <s>Along the path, mosques will call ṣalāt al-kusūf, the prayer of the eclipse — a reminder, in the Prophet's own words, that eclipses are signs of God and not omens about the affairs of men.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In Jammu, a panel headed by India's registrar general and census commissioner has arrived for a three-day visit to study what the home ministry calls demographic change from illegal immigration and other abnormal reasons.</s> <s>The composition is the finding: the officer who runs the census is being sent to investigate the population of a disputed territory, and Assam's citizens' register — the working precedent — left roughly one point nine million people off a list.</s> <s>Once a state commissions a finding that a population is abnormal, documentation demands and voter-roll revisions follow, and the burden of proof lands on people who've lived somewhere for generations.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Austrian judges in Vienna have now refused four of the eighteen names on Tajikistan's extradition dossier, finding the charges against them political.</s> <s>This is transnational repression by paperwork — an authoritarian state doesn't need to reach its critics abroad if it can persuade Interpol and foreign prosecutors to do it, since a red notice works as a bank freeze and a travel ban even when a court eventually throws it out.</s> <s>Fourteen names are still pending, and the exiles named in them wait in a legal limbo that costs years whichever way it ends.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Osun state's governor, Ademola Adeleke, says a serving federal minister has openly threatened to rig Saturday's governorship vote in Nigeria — an allegation from his own spokesperson, not yet independently confirmed.</s> <s>What makes the charge structurally plausible is that the electoral commission's leadership and the police both answer to Abuja, so an opposition governor contests an election whose referees are appointed by his rival's government.</s> <s>Four days out, an accusation this specific is either evidence that demands action now or a pre-emptive case against a result... and both carry consequences.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Turkey's parliament voted four hundred and sixty-eight to eighty-eight to suspend prosecutions of Kurdistan Workers' Party fighters who disarm, for a period of five to ten years.</s> <s>Three international outlets couldn't agree on what to call it — peace, a pardon, a limited amnesty — and the gap between those words is the story, because a forty-year insurgency that killed some forty thousand people is being closed by a statute written as procedure rather than as settlement.</s> <s>The law specifies weapons handover and legal status; it says nothing about language rights, local governance, or the release of Abdullah Öcalan.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Turkish foreign minister Hakan Fidan says Egypt could join the mutual-defence pact signed in Mecca by Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey once technical issues are resolved.</s> <s>A bilateral pact is an alliance; a four-state pact spanning Anatolia, the Hejaz, the Indus and the Nile would be a bloc, and the fifty-seven-member Islamic conference has never had one with a military instrument behind it.</s> <s>Its power lies in what it refuses to state — whether Pakistan's nuclear deterrent extends to Saudi territory — an undefined guarantee that deters two rivals at once while committing Islamabad to nothing in writing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>On Warraq Island in the Nile, families ended their sit-in against eviction after a single day, in exchange for a promise from Egyptian security officials to restore water, power and lighting.</s> <s>Security officials, not city officials, made that promise — which means there's no document, no deadline, and no agency anyone can hold to it.</s> <s>Residents meet Friday to decide what to do if nothing arrives.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The Karachi stock exchange fell for a second day as Brent crude traded near eighty-nine dollars a barrel, with talks over the Strait of Hormuz stalled.</s> <s>Read it as a transmission line rather than a market report: Pakistan buys nearly all its crude and gas through that strait and pays in dollars it doesn't earn, so every dollar on the barrel widens the deficit, pressures the rupee, and eventually lands as a power tariff on a household in Multan.</s> <s>It's a country that's neither party to the war nor able to leave the route.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Lahore, Pakistan's farmers' alliance has demanded Punjab's chief minister resign and threatened a march on Rawalpindi.</s> <s>Note the destination — the garrison city, not the capital — which tells you where petitioners believe decisions are actually made, and the grievance behind it is a price scissors: the wheat support price was withdrawn under an International Monetary Fund condition while fertiliser, diesel and tube-well electricity stayed at subsidised-era costs.</s> <s>A planting decision taken this autumn by growers who lost money last season becomes next year's import bill and next year's flour price.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia's largest online retailer, Wildberries, is shifting stock into Kazakhstan as Ukrainian drones keep striking its warehouses at home.</s> <s>A company can't move its customers, so it moves the shelf — and the shelf lands in a state that hasn't chosen a side, bringing construction and transit fees along with secondary-sanctions exposure for Kazakh banks and builders.</s> <s>When a war reaches the logistics layer, the neighbours get annexed into the supply chain long before anyone crosses a border.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nvidia has arranged roughly five hundred billion dollars in financing for artificial-intelligence chips through six large lenders.</s> <s>The structure is the point: Nvidia books the revenue immediately, while the debt sits with private-credit firms whose money comes from pension funds and insurers — meaning the exposure ends up with retirees, not on the chipmaker's balance sheet.</s> <s>Nvidia hasn't said whether it would step in if that debt turned bad.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Off the coast of Oman, an oil slick from a sanctioned tanker has grown to four hundred square kilometres and now sits seven kilometres from shore.</s> <s>The vessel flies Cameroon's flag while its owner and manager are both based in China — the flag-of-convenience arrangement that lets a ship's real controllers stay several jurisdictions away from any cleanup bill.</s> <s>Oman says the slick could reach Ras Madrakah within two days.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Sea surface temperatures hit twenty point nine six degrees Celsius in July, the highest ever recorded.</s> <s>Oceans have absorbed roughly ninety percent of the heat trapped since industrialisation, which means a warmer Indian Ocean intensifies cyclones and shifts monsoon rains for two billion people regardless of what emissions do next.</s> <s>A developing El Niño is building on top of that record, and its effects are still ahead of us.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>New archaeoastronomy work argues the Neolithic people who reached Malta crossed roughly a hundred kilometres of open Mediterranean out of sight of land, navigating by stars, a thousand years before the pyramids.</s> <s>An island that far offshore can't be reached by drifting, and the technique — a star that rises at a fixed bearing gives a repeatable course with no instrument at all — appears independently in the Pacific, the Indian Ocean and the Arabian Sea.</s> <s>The Arab navigators who later formalised it, Ibn Mājid and the altitude measure taken on a kamal, weren't inventing a method so much as writing down one that had already been sailed for millennia.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers studying Taiwan's Milun Fault have found that grinding rock alone can split water into hydrogen.</s> <s>Fracturing breaks silicate bonds and leaves unpaired electrons that pull water apart, which ties the fuel supply of deep microbial life to tectonic stress rather than to biology.</s> <s>The finding raises a question the paper doesn't answer: how much of the planet's hydrogen is made this way, everywhere the ground moves.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Procurement records show United States Immigration and Customs Enforcement paying LexisNexis six point seven million dollars for bulk personal data, routed into a Palantir system.</s> <s>The purchase buys records the agency couldn't lawfully compel — addresses, phone histories, utility hookups, vehicle records — because a warrant requirement binds a government's own collection, not its shopping, so the constitutional check disappears at the point of sale rather than being overruled.</s> <s>The same brokers sell the same categories of data on residents of Pakistan, Nigeria, Egypt and the Gulf, and no immigration status is required to be in the file.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Federal Bureau of Investigation and South Korea have jointly warned that the Gunra ransomware group is breaching critical infrastructure through flaws in widely deployed firewalls.</s> <s>A firewall is bought specifically to be the boundary, so this isn't a breach of the perimeter but a breach by it — these appliances face the internet by design, run vendor firmware customers can't inspect, and hold the credentials for everything behind them.</s> <s>The same models sit in front of hospitals in Lahore, ports in Alexandria and banks in Jakarta, and an English-language advisory is the only warning most of those operators will get.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Amazon is funding a gas plant at Fort Stockton, Texas, whose thirty-five turbines could emit thirty-three million tons of carbon dioxide a year, making it the single largest climate polluter in the country.</s> <s>Building power on-site is what makes that possible: it bypasses the interconnection queue, the transmission planning and the emissions review a utility-scale plant would face.</s> <s>The company says it'll offset the emissions, without saying how.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In California, the security-robot company Knightscope has lost at least thirteen of its twenty-one deployments and is now rehiring the human guards it was built to replace.</s> <s>One machine patrolled Dublin for ten months and identified zero incidents before its contract ended — a useful measure of what automation actually delivered against what it promised.</s> <s>The firm carries two hundred and seventy-three million dollars in debt, and has bought a guard company to pair humans with the robots.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>